1. SYSTEM OVERVIEW & CORE ANALOGY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This system acts as an autonomous multi-attribute clearinghouse (similar to a 
Cloud Compute Spot-Instance Auction Engine or Uber Surge Matching system) for 
supply-chain invoices. 

Rather than functioning as a passive comparison rate site (like a loan aggregator), 
the system continuously matches three core market actors:
  - Sellers (Suppliers/Vendors): Entities with unpaid invoices seeking rapid liquidity 
    (e.g., within 2-4 hours to meet payroll) who trade off interest rates for speed/advance rates.
  - Buyers (Enterprise Clients): Corporations holding 30/60/90-day payment terms who 
    require payment verification and single-payee settlement guarantees.
  - Credit Owners (Banks/NBFCs/Private Funds): Institutional liquidity pools seeking 
    yield subject to rigid portfolio constraints (e.g., max $5M per sector, minimum credit score).

The platform coordinates an end-to-end autonomous loop:
Invoice Upload -> 3-Way Verification -> Risk Pricing -> Bidding Auction -> Multi-Attribute Matching -> Disbursal -> Escrow Settlement -> Adaptive Learning.

