2. TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE & AWS CLOUD FOOTPRINT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Deployment Strategy: Serverless & Containerized AWS Infrastructure prioritizing sub-second matching, high concurrency, and non-blocking background workers.

Architecture Stack:
  - Edge/Routing: AWS Route 53 + CloudFront CDN.
  - Application Layer: AWS ECS Fargate hosting containerized Next.js (App Router) & Node.js backend services.
  - Asynchronous Execution: Amazon SQS (Message Queuing) triggering AWS Lambda functions for background tasks (OCR processing, verification webhooks, and AI voice calls).
  - Database & Caching:
      * Primary: Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 (PostgreSQL) enforcing ACID transactions for invoices, bids, and audit trails.
      * In-Memory Cache: Amazon ElastiCache (Redis) handling distributed locking (SETNX) to prevent race conditions during concurrent bid lockouts.
  - Encrypted Storage: Amazon S3 (KMS Encrypted) for storing PDF invoices, signed delivery notes, and ElevenLabs verification audio logs.
  - Security & Secrets: AWS Secrets Manager storing API keys for ElevenLabs, Nexus AI, and external webhooks.

